# queen-trap-fix.patch — quiet-reply queen-trap blindness, qsearch evasion v1
#
# Root cause (bench diagnostics 2026-11-27, benches/diagnostics/README.md):
# an attacked queen's defences are its own flight moves, which are QUIET, so
# capture-only quiescence never sees the queen captured at a flight square; the
# entire quiet-reply trap sequence hides beyond the horizon (RFP/futility can
# additionally cut the quiet reply at non-PV nodes). 8 of 13 adjudicated E4
# falls are "needle" cases (1-2 trap-allowing moves among 33-49 legal).
#
# Fix: in quiesce_core, when the side to move has an ATTACKED queen, keep the
# full legal move list (like check evasions) and skip stand-pat - "doing
# nothing" there loses the queen on the opponent's next capture. Nodes without
# an attacked queen are unchanged (capture-only, stand-pat, delta pruning).
#
# Apply on the frozen campaign target cb7242c (or any tree with the same
# quiesce_core). DEVELOPED AFTER the ENGINE-4 gate decision per the fix
# discipline in benches/diagnostics/README.md; verified by engine-probe.yml
# (compile + release tests + bench + the 13-case fixed-depth probe).
